# LMS Project Core

You MUST follow this architecture. Do not introduce patterns outside these boundaries.

## Stack

- Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript (strict), Tailwind CSS v4
- i18n: `next-intl` only — locales `en` and `ja`, default `ja`
- Forms: `react-hook-form` + `zod` via `UiForm`
- State: `zustand` when needed; prefer local/server state first
- Icons: `react-icons` only
- Path alias: `@/*` → `src/*`

Before writing Next.js code, read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` — this project uses Next.js 16 with breaking API changes.

## Directory Layout

```
src/
  app/[locale]/           # Route groups by role: (auth), (learner), (operator), (creator), (company-admin)
  features/{role}/{name}/ # Business logic + colocated messages/
  components/
    ui/{name}/            # Reusable primitives (button, input, select, …)
    form/                 # UiForm + field wrappers
    layouts/              # Role layouts + layout messages
  i18n/                   # routing, navigation, message-loader, registry, types
  messages/{en,ja}/       # Global dictionaries: common, navigation, validation
  lib/utils/              # cn() and shared utilities
```

## Routing Rules

- App pages are thin wrappers — import and render a feature component only.
- Use `Link`, `useRouter`, `redirect` from `@/i18n/navigation` — NEVER from `next/navigation` or `next/link` directly.
- Role routes: `/learner/*`, `/operator/*`, `/creator`, `/company-admin`, auth at `/`.

## Import Conventions

- UI primitives: `@/components/ui` or `@/components/ui/{name}`
- Forms: `@/components/form`, `@/components/form/fields/*`
- Features: `@/features/{role}/{name}/{name}` (or auth component path)
- Utils: `@/lib/utils`

## Refusals

- Do NOT add new UI libraries (MUI, Chakra, shadcn CLI, etc.).
- Do NOT add alternative i18n, routing, or form libraries.
- Do NOT put business logic in `src/app/` pages.
- Do NOT create files outside the directory layout above without explicit user request.
